module wied-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ SentencingScheduled }

// The Eastern District of Wisconsin's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). The
// Criminal Rules of Part C govern criminal and petty offense proceedings
// (E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 1). In a proceeding that needs no indictment,
// a deadline that runs from arraignment on an indictment runs instead from
// the entry of a not-guilty plea on the trial document (Criminal L. R.
// 58(a)(1)); `ArraignedOnIndictment` is that event too. No trigger carries
// a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the manner of
// service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods counted in business days stay in notes, since lit/core's FRCrimP
// 45(a) rule counts calendar days: under the Expanded Discovery Policy,
// grand jury transcripts of the government's trial witnesses are made
// available no later than 1 business day before trial, and the defense
// discloses FRCrimP 16(b)(1)(C) material not later than 5 business days
// before trial absent good cause (Criminal L. R. 16(a)(4)).
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: the judge
// in each criminal case issues the FRCrimP 5(f) Brady order (Criminal L. R.
// 5); in an unusually complex case the government notifies the Clerk when
// the indictment or information is filed, and a pretrial scheduling
// conference may set the case's deadlines (Criminal L. R. 12(a)(1), (2));
// absent such a conference the government uses its best efforts to make
// discovery available at arraignment or within 5 days after it (Criminal
// L. R. 12(a)(3)), a best-efforts target rather than a deadline; a
// corporate disclosure statement is filed with the first appearance
// (Criminal L. R. 12.4(b)); a motion to compel discovery states the
// conference held (Criminal L. R. 16(b)); grand jury materials (Criminal L.
// R. 6), presentence report confidentiality (Criminal L. R. 32(a)), sealed
// hearings (Criminal L. R. 49) and misdemeanors and petty offenses
// (Criminal L. R. 58) set no other period.
//
// The earlier E.D. Wis. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// The defendant is arraigned on an indictment, or, where no indictment is
/// necessary, a not-guilty plea is entered on the trial document (E.D. Wis.
/// Criminal L. R. 12(b)(1), 16.1(a), 58(a)(1)).
event ArraignedOnIndictment()
/// The date on which a Rule 12(b)(3) motion is due (E.D. Wis. Criminal L.
/// R. 12(b)(2)).
event PretrialMotionDue()
/// The date on which the non-movant's response is due (E.D. Wis. Criminal
/// L. R. 12(b)(3)).
event PretrialResponseDue()
/// A motion seeking an evidentiary hearing is filed (E.D. Wis. Criminal L.
/// R. 12(c)).
event EvidentiaryHearingMotionFiled()
/// A motion to reassign a criminal case as related is filed (E.D. Wis.
/// Criminal L. R. 13(b)).
event ReassignmentMotionFiled()
/// Trial commences (E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16(a)(4), (5)).
event TrialCommences()

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(b)(1): absent a court order, every motion
/// raising an issue described in FRCrimP 12(b)(3) is filed within 20 days
/// after arraignment on an indictment, with a supporting memorandum or a
/// certificate that none will be filed.
deadline pretrial-motions: 20.days after ArraignedOnIndictment() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(b); E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 58(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(b)(2): absent a court order, the non-movant
/// may file a response within 10 days from the date the motion is due, or
/// files a statement that it will not respond.
deadline pretrial-motion-response: 10.days after PretrialMotionDue() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(b)(3): absent a court order, the movant may
/// file a reply within 5 days from the date the response is due.
deadline pretrial-motion-reply: 5.days after PretrialResponseDue() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(c): the non-movant may file a response
/// opposing an evidentiary hearing, stating why it is unnecessary, within
/// 3 days after the filing of the motion seeking one.
deadline evidentiary-hearing-opposition: 3.days after EvidentiaryHearingMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 12(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 13(b): any objection to a motion to reassign a
/// criminal case as related is filed within 7 days of the filing of the
/// motion.
deadline reassignment-objection: 7.days after ReassignmentMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 13(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16.1(a): as soon after indictment as
/// practicable, and in no event more than 14 days after arraignment, the
/// attorney for the government and defense counsel confer regarding
/// discovery.
deadline discovery-conference: 14.days after ArraignedOnIndictment() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16(a)(4): unless the Court orders otherwise,
/// when the government follows its Expanded Discovery Policy it discloses
/// FRCrimP 16(a)(1)(G) material not later than 15 days before trial,
/// absent good cause for later disclosure.
deadline expert-disclosure: 15.days before TrialCommences() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16(a)(5): if the government follows the
/// Expanded Discovery Policy, the defense discloses FRCrimP 16(b)(1)(A) and
/// (B) material as soon as reasonably practicable and not later than 15
/// days before trial, absent good cause for later disclosure.
deadline defense-reciprocal-disclosure: 15.days before TrialCommences() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 16(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 32(b): when the defendant has waived the
/// FRCrimP 32(e)(2) time limits, objections to the presentence report are
/// submitted in writing to the Probation Department and served on the
/// opposing party at least 10 days before the scheduled sentencing, unless
/// the Court orders otherwise.
deadline psr-objections-on-waiver: 10.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "E.D. Wis. Criminal L. R. 32(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
